At the 2007 [[Shanghai Motor Show]], Buick debuted a [[concept car|concept]] coupe named Riviera, based on the [[GM Epsilon II platform]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Nunez |first=Alex |url= http://www.autoblog.com/2007/04/14/shanghai-motor-show-preview-buick-riviera-concept/ |title=Shanghai Motor Show Preview: Buick Riviera Concept |website=Autoblog.com |date=2007-04-14 |access-date=2011-09-13}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= http://news.carjunky.com/the-buick-riviera-concept-cdf465.shtml |title=The Buick Riviera Concept : Car Makes And Models |website=News.carjunky.com |access-date=2011-09-13}}</ref> The concept was later shown at the [[North American International Auto Show#2008|2008 North American International Auto Show]].

It was designed by the [[Pan Asia Technical Automotive Center]] ([[PATAC]]). The design was inspired by classic Buicks, ancient Chinese artifacts, and modern electronic icons. It includes "icy green" backlighting, Shell Blue body, [[gull-wing door]]s, a 2+2 seating configuration, and 21-inch 10-spoke forged aluminum wheels.
